WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just hit six years,
your anniversary.

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations, and the show.
-We did.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.741
-I'm sure the same question
people like me get asked,

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.110
you get asked, "It probably
feels a little bit longer

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.245
than six years after everything
that's happened."

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It feels
like my entire lifetime.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It really does.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.916
I mean,
particularly the last few years.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every week is a year.
-Yeah.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:21.021
I think that's about right.
-Someone the other day --

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
Today, we were
having a segment meeting,

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
and someone's like,
"When the Mueller came --

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:25.892 line:92%
When the Barr report came out,

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.560 size:81% position:41%
you know, Barr letter
came out 10 days ago,"

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Stop it."
-Yeah.

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:31.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was only 10 days ago.
-Yeah.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:33.600 size:81% position:41%
-And what's been nice
is you have found time

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.470
to talk about other things,
and you hosted a town hall

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez.
-Yeah.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was about
the Green New Deal.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think, you know, again,
something that

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the surface,
people have heard a lot about

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
but maybe
not much more than that.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. It's funny.
It's become this --

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:50.784 line:92%
instantly became this, like,

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:52.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
cartoonish villain
for the right.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:55.221
I mean, Trump TV talks about it,
like, all of the time.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But very few were people --

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
People talking
about the politics.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:00:59.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were talking about
the criticism.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.594
Very few people were talking
about it on its own terms,

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is not to say like,
"Oh, this is the way to go."

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just, "What is the thing?
How would it work?

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.399 line:92%
What's the theory behind it?"

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.568
So, we wanted to kind of
take some time to talk about it.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And did you find being in
a townhall format

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
you got the sense that there
are people out there

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.206 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
now more than ever

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
who accept climate change
as a serious issue?

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:18.144
-I think -- It is one of the
biggest generational divides

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:18.912 size:78% position:39% line:92%
in American politics.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we did this thing,
it was great.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like 900 people.
It was in the Bronx, which is

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
where Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez
is from.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.351 line:92%
It's from where I'm from.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.253
We did it in the hospital
I was born in, actually.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Funnily enough.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, now it's getting creepy.
-Yeah.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:34.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
In the L&amp;D wing,
which was weird for everyone.

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.529 size:78% position:39%
-No, we did it there.
And one of the things

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.565
I think you've seen that's been
transformational,

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.733 size:88% position:44%
particularly in the last
three to five years is,

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's just grassroots energy
around this issue.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:44.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for a long time,
it was like,

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.040
"Oh, this thing that's happening
off in the future,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we should
do something about it."

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
But there are people
who understand

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we are on
the front edge of it now,

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we have to meet
the challenge now.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I certainly enjoyed it.
Some people did not.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:02:00.253
You mentioned -- or, you alluded
to the fact that, you know,

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.688 size:88% position:44% line:92%
the Green New Deal is --

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:04.824
Fox News has certainly framed it
as being very problematic.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they do seem to have
an obsession with AOC

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a creator of bad things.
-Yes.

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:12.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Tucker Carlson, though,
focused on you.

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:12.899 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He did.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And had this to say about you
in the townhall.

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Chris Hayes
is what every man would be

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.808
if feminists ever achieved
absolute power in this country.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:26.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
Apologetic, bespectacled,
and deeply, deeply concerned

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:27.547 size:75% position:38% line:92%
about global warming

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:30.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the patriarchal systems
that cause it.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of all the things, the idea --
-Bespectacled!

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:37.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Bespectacled!
-Yes.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:39.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The idea that
if the feminists take over,

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're all gonna
have to wear glasses?

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-No.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:46.032
It's true.
The most macho thing you can do

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
is drive your car
without your glasses.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:50.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is --
That is peak masculinity.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:53.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Also, I don't know anything
about Tucker Carlson,

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he looks like a guy
who needs glasses

00:02:55.408 --> 00:03:00.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it's constantly like...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe he'd be, like,
a little -- maybe that's it.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
We think he's like,
"Why is he so flummoxed?"

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, he can barely
read the cue cards.

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:09.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He needs the feminist
takeover to happen sooner.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:13.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that he did not quite
recognize the context

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
of that comment
outside the confines

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the bubble of Fox News.
-Right.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
That it would escape and be --
yeah.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It did escape.
And it led to, basically,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
the best 24 hours
of social media of my life.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really nice.
-It's like my birthday.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.840 line:92%
I was like, "Oh, thanks."

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you're active
on social media,

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.410 line:92%
and you have War on Dad Bod.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.445
And I know a lot of dads
out there, me included --

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:33.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, we're --
-We just think it's great

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:36.282 size:78% position:39%
that you're out there
fighting the dad bod.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.818 line:92%
And, so, this is your Instagram.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:39.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you want to read that
for us right there?

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:44.157
-"Every quarter the femnarcist
junta requires all adult males

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
to present themselves
for a fitness inspection.

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:49.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
Failure to pass
results in summary execution."

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.531 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:54.534
-That was --
I mean, I will say all things --

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
Yeah.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:04:02.609
All things being equal, a zinger
from Tucker Carlson to you

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:03.543 line:92%
is actually a lot more fun

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:07.113 size:84% position:42%
than a lot of the stuff
that comes out of Fox.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I wish it was all --
-Oh, yeah. No.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was delightful.
-All zingers like that.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly, yes.
Very low-stakes situation.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That was --
You know, if they were just

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:15.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
going after you
instead immigrants,

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be like,
"I'll take that trade, yeah."

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:18.591 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:23.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
But do you have time
to consume much Fox News?

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:24.364 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, I don't.

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:26.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you do see
things across your feed.

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:29.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we have this thing
where it's on.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.104 line:92%
You know, it's on in the office.

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:33.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got the three
big cable news stations,

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you sort of see
what's on air on CNN,

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
partly as a sort of
point of comparison --

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:37.543 line:92%
What are people covering?

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:39.879
What are the general stories
that are driving that day?

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:42.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will watch stuff online
sometimes.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't have
a huge appetite for it.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:45.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:49.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I do end up
seeing a fair amount.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:51.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Yeah.

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.925 line:92%
And do you have a sense that --

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.695
Are you surprised
by what you see or is it now --

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:56.229 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
have you come --

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:58.731
I mean, does it stop being
surprising at some point?

00:04:58.731 --> 00:04:59.399 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No. You know what?

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:01.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
What's sort of fascinating
about it, it's like,

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.136 size:84% position:42% line:92%
it is to news what like

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
a Broadway set
is to an actual apartment.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.375
You look at it, and you're like,
"That looks -- That kind of --

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:12.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
That sort of looks like --
That sort of looks like news."

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:16.516
-But it's, like, this fabricated
ersatz version of it.

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And everyone sort of

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:21.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
does all the stuff
inside the playacting set

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:24.691
that is this little sort of
universe they've created.

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it's sort of unnerving
and it's surreal.

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:30.330
And I think, to the degree
that people exist inside

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:33.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
just that world,
it could be really toxic.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:37.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. I think we've found out
that that is truth.

00:05:37.437 --> 00:05:40.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would also say --
Very true.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:41.607 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the oranges
of a lot of our problems.

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:45.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. It really is.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:46.879 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's a callback.

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:50.883 line:92%
That's a guest doing a callback.

